{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: make gs refuse a bad act before signing it, and answer a bad invocation with usage.\n\nWhy. Across 52 local agent sessions on this workroom, 272 acts were appended and then ruled ineffective by the fold, and 681 gs invocations were refused. The fold's top reasons are shape and authority mistakes: actor may not supersede target (68), ratify target is not effective (33), artifact state requires body.path (26), report cites a request other than the one its promise answers (24), report has no promise or request (21), dangling promise has no request (21), ratify target is unknown (19). Half the CLI refusals are about command shape: 118 --help calls, 77 undefined-flag guesses (--target, --as, --text, --server, --idempotency-key on commands that take positionals), 90 missing required flags, 55 malformed event ids. Every one of these cost an agent a re-read of SKILL.md or a reference page and a refile; a permanent ineffective record also stays in the log forever. The fold already knows each reason; the CLI just does not ask before it signs.\n\nOutcome. gs state, gs batch, gs ratify and gs supersede run the fold's admission decision for the prospective act against the current projection before signing, and refuse with the fold's own reason and a one-line fix when the act would be ineffective. Reasons that depend on a race (a basis retired between preflight and append) stay with the fold. A refusal for an undefined flag, a missing required flag, a positional given as a flag, or a malformed event id prints the command's usage with one worked example. Existing behaviour on admitted acts is unchanged; the fold's rules do not move.","body":{"branch":"request/refuse-before-signing","conditions":"1. Before signing, gs state and gs batch evaluate the prospective act with the same fold code the resident runs (no second rule set) and refuse when the decision would be ineffective, printing the fold's reason verbatim plus a one-line fix; ratify and supersede do the same for target unknown, target not effective, not ratifiable, actor lacks role, and actor may not supersede target (naming who may). 2. The check is skippable with one flag for the deliberate replay of a refused shape, and it never changes what an admitted act contains. 3. An undefined flag, a missing required flag, a flag given where a positional is expected, or an event reference that does not parse prints usage with one example and exits non-zero without touching the log or a key. 4. Each refusal class from the list in the request text has a test that shows the act is refused before any key is loaded and nothing is appended, and one that shows the same act admitted when its precondition is satisfied. 5. docs/reference/gs/state.md, batch.md, ratify.md and supersede.md document the preflight and its skip flag; docs/reference/architecture.md is updated if a layer contract moves. 6. go test ./... green at the exact head; independent review by codex; ratified; landed on main and pushed.","target_head":"c3cc0e4479f9d0e3a5f04e20ecdcfecdc492ecd9","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}